Z||000000||porridgeman||05-11-2001||01:20 PM||||Can any one tell me if a guy can buy Hinge Pin Rollers for an 86 GT without having to buy the complete lower hinge assembly?<BR>Got some of the shelf from the "HELP" rack <BR>but they are to long on the shaft.It said they wre for GM 82-88,maybe a pick-up.<BR> TIA<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-11-2001||10:09 PM||||Are you replaceing them because they were bad, or becuase your door is sagging?<P>If it is your door sagging and the rollers work fine, replace the pins and bushings, and the door will tighten up.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||05-13-2001||12:45 AM||||porridgeman - I couldnt respond to your email, sent you a reply and then it bounced back to me.<P>Anyway, what I was going to say would be to check out your local pontiac dealer.  It is quite possible that the roller pins arent Fiero specific, they are probably used on other models from that era.  If they dont turn out any luck, try a junkyard and pull a good one from a wrecked Fiero.  If you still can't get on, post a topic in the mall and maybe someone either has one lying around or is willing to pull one off of one of thier parts cars for you.<P>Good luck!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
